# GitHub Pages

Production build must use `_config_prod.yml` (`url=https://gervisbermudez.github.io`, `baseurl=/site`). CI: `.github/workflows/static.yml` runs `bundle exec jekyll build --config _config_prod.yml` then deploys `_site` to `gh-pages`.

Local `_config.yml` keeps `url` and `baseurl` empty. Do not copy prod `baseurl` into the local config.

CSS/asset 404s on github.io are almost always missing `| relative_url`, not a missing `/site` prefix. Hardcoding `/site` “fixes” prod and breaks local (and can double-prefix).

Plugins (do not drop; listed in both configs + Gemfile): `jekyll-feed`, `jekyll-paginate`, `jekyll-seo-tag`, `jekyll-sitemap`.

Do not add gems or change the deploy workflow unless the user asked.
